# Integer128 addition at the type boundary

Adds 7 at the upper boundary of the 128-bit range to verify the sum lands
exactly on the int128 maximum, then adds 7 to the mirrored negative value
to verify it stays in range. Every operand carries an int128 annotation so
both cases exercise same-type addition.

>>> source
left: int128 = 170141183460469231731687303715884105720
right: int128 = 7
neg_left: int128 = -170141183460469231731687303715884105720

// Verifies addition reaching exactly the int128 maximum.
boundary_sum: int128 = left + right
print(boundary_sum)

// Verifies addition of a negative operand staying in range.
negative_sum: int128 = neg_left + right
print(negative_sum)

<<< stdout
170141183460469231731687303715884105727
-170141183460469231731687303715884105713

<<< stderr
